WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.350
Mumbai, 2025: about 27,000
people per square kilometer.

2
00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:08.970
Perth: fewer than 2,000.

3
00:00:09.020 --> 00:00:12.790
Of the world's 50 least dense
cities of a million or more,

4
00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:15.510
21 were in the USA.

5
00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:19.530
So why do some cities spread
out while others build up?

6
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:22.370
Is it just that bigger
countries have more land?

7
00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:26.350
In this mission, you'll compare low,
medium and high density housing,

8
00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:28.950
and how each one uses land.

9
00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:31.750
Then you'll explore how what people value,

10
00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:35.050
like privacy, a yard,
or living close to work,

11
00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.290
shows up in what they build.

12
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:42.370
Your mission: explain why some cities
spread out in houses with yards while others

13
00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.200
stack people in towers.
